    "notes": "Q1243401/way90446374 identifies the ruin precinct rather than a solid modern building. The standard map supplies the stepped main-hall footprint, two large L-shaped enclosure strips, seven small ancillary remnants, a west detached ruin and the circular well. Internal+U runs northeast; the paired main front faces southwest toward the river. The low front, broad main hall and narrowing rear arrangement follow the mapped vertices. The Crocodile Museum and small later kiosk remain independent, with a0.1mm numerical margin at shared mask edges. Pinned small standard2026-10-14 PMTiles/Mapzen extract. Main and forecourt decks use separate visualization datums above the local coarse grid, with retaining foundations and a stepped transition. Enclosure remnants follow the standard native grade. Ground and Nile water stay native, with no ground/water cutout. The well is a shallow sealed mouth/basin above the native grade rather than a claim to its surveyed underground shaft. Pinned small standard2026-10-14 PMTiles/Mapzen extract. Main and forecourt decks use separate visualization datums above the local coarse grid, with retaining foundations and a stepped transition. Enclosure remnants follow the standard native grade. Ground and Nile water stay native, with no ground/water cutout. The well is a shallow sealed mouth/basin above the native grade rather than a claim to its surveyed underground shaft. Both independent in-tile buildings, including the Crocodile Museum and later kiosk, remain unchanged. Thirteen authored map records are replaced; a 0.00069323m² native enclosure seam remains at the protected kiosk boundary, and other remnants are below 1e-7m². Original terrain and the fixture’s native Nile geometry remain unchanged. Failed loading restores all 15 original map records and eviction frees model geometry."
